et_debt_ebitda":true,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":77.8,"_gate_accruals":-0.0315255183916289,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":41.1,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.1692755602189061,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":65.9,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.007331160041715648,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":0.013333545698656274,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":6.7,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.37279200994580075,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":37.9,"_gate_incr_roic":0.04309500483364004,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":31.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.05482576944666739,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":15.1,"_gate_pool_share":-0.06952964411807983,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":12.2,"_gate_rev_durability":0.010042115476630809,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":30.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.02102041134407684,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":14.5,"_gate_margins":0.009080437321274134,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":59.1,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.07025779435273813,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":89.2,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.7534673846136404,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.004854309888277641,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":91.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.02869,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":19.1,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Hub Group, Inc., a supply chain solutions provider, offers transportation and logistics management services in North America. It operates in two segments, Intermodal and Transportation Solutions (ITS), and Logistics. The ITS segment offers intermodal and dedicated trucking services, including freight transportation, truckload, less-than-truckload, flatbed, temperature-controlled, and dedicated and regional trucking services. The Logistics segment provides transportation management, freight brokerage, shipment optimization, load consolidation, mode selection, carrier management, load planning and execution, warehousing, fulfillment, cross-docking, and consolidation and final mile delivery services. It also provides trucking transportation services, including dry van, expedited, less-than-truckload, and refrigerated and flatbed services. As of December 31, 2024, the company operated a fleet of approximately 2,300 tractors, 3,200 employee drivers, 500 independent owner-operators, and 4,700 trailers; and owned approximately 50,000 dry and 53-foot containers, as well as 900 refrigerated 53-foot containers. It serves a range of industries, including retail, consumer products, automotive, and durable goods. The company was founded in 1971 and is headquartered in Oak Brook, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David P. Yeager | Chairman & CEO | Age 72 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2024)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Revenue per employee of $598K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $22K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Hub Group, Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $1.4B market cap on $3.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, and 12% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $144M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.87\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 9.7\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 7.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 2.9% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Industrials peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Industrials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 60% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 58% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(HUBG) Volatility Zones as Tactical Triggers","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/40/HUBG_Volatility_Zones_as_Tactical_Triggers_112526022601_1795591561.html","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795591561.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How Investors May Respond To Hub Group (HUBG) Conditional Listing Approval","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/investors-may-respond-hub-group-051222997.html","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795065142.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.904,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["regulatory"]},{"title":"Hub Group Extends Financial Statement Submission Deadline with Fourth Credit Agreement Amendment","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/hub-group-extends-financial-statement-submission-deadline-with-fourth-credit-agreement-amendment","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795642744.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.743,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Hub Group granted another extension to file late quarterly results","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/hub-group-granted-another-extension-142600308.html","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795616760.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.226,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Hub Group backs UP-NS merger; Prime Inc. urges rejection, Honda raises competition concerns","source"